# The toll book (TSC_FactorsLedger, ledger chain): the reveal that the
# toll crew reports to somebody, and the somebody signs in a guild hand.
# Both lore approaches open this; the spot sets TSC_LedgerRead.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_FactorsLedger

== start ==
The entries are the wrong shape for banditry. Every caravan this crew took is written in days BEFORE they took it: route, escort count, load itemized down to the barrel.

They did not scout. They were told.

* [Check the margins.] -> margins

== margins ==
One hand has initialed every page, cramped in the margin beside the crew's sprawl. A clerk's hand, chancery-trained, with a particular hooked terminal on the final stroke.

{PLAYER} has seen that hook before. It is on the company's own guild charter.

* "A toll crew that gets audited." -> audited

== audited ==
Bandits do not keep books. Men who must SHOW their books keep them, and show them to whoever signs the margin - and this margin is signed from inside the guild.

The pages come out of the stitching clean. The signature now belongs to somebody who can be found.

* [Pocket the pages.] -> end
